{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Pre-review sweep — re-measured against `origin/main` `403719c01ce`\n\nThe plan cites base `083620b0`, which is an ancestor of current main. The reasoning here is sound and I verified its load-bearing claims; the citations have drifted, **one AC cannot pass as written**, and **part of the work has already landed**.\n\n---\n\n### 1. AC1 is unsatisfiable — the grep returns 30 hits, only 9 in scope\n\nRunning AC1 verbatim on current main:\n\n```\ngit grep -n '_ALIASES\\b\\|_LEGACY_ENV_ALIASES\\|_map_legacy_env' -- src tests scripts\n→ 30 hits across 18 files\n```\n\n`_ALIASES\\b` binds only the *right* edge of the token, so it matches any identifier **ending** in `_ALIASES`. The 30 hits decompose into 7 distinct identifiers:\n\n| identifier | hits | in scope? |\n|---|---:|---|\n| `_HIDDEN_ALIASES` | 11 | no — CLI help router |\n| `_ALIASES` | 10 | **yes** |\n| `_REMOVED_SIMPLE_CLI_ALIASES` | 2 | no — CLI help router |\n| `_EDIT_FLAG_ALIASES` | 2 | no — `composer_edit.py` |\n| `_DEPRECATED_PROVIDER_ALIASES` | 2 | no — `llm/providers.py` |\n| `_ARCH_ALIASES` | 2 | no — `scripts/ensure_pandoc.py` (pandoc arch map) |\n| `_LEGACY_ENV_ALIASES` | 1 | yes, but it is a **docstring mention**, not code |\n\n21 of 30 hits are live, unrelated code that must stay. **AC1 can never be satisfied**, no matter how completely the story is implemented — it would fail on `_ARCH_ALIASES` in a pandoc download helper.\n\n**A tightened regex is necessary but not sufficient.** Binding both edges still leaves three hits, because the test **fixture corpora** embed prose that quotes the deleted symbols:\n\n- `tests/fixtures/cloud_adf_corpus/bodies_00.json:29` — contains `_config_sources._map_legacy_env` inside a captured ticket comment\n- `tests/fixtures/dc_wiki_corpus/prose.json:109` — contains `_HIDDEN_ALIASES`\n- `tests/fixtures/dc_wiki_corpus/table.json:13` — same body as the ADF corpus\n\nThese are frozen corpus data for the Jira/Confluence renderers. They are not references to the symbols and must not be edited. AC1 therefore needs **both** whole-identifier binding **and** a `:(exclude)tests/fixtures` pathspec:\n\n```\ngit grep -nE '(^|[^A-Za-z0-9_])(_ALIASES|_LEGACY_ENV_ALIASES|_map_legacy_env)\\b' \\\n  -- src tests scripts ':(exclude)tests/fixtures'\n```\n\nWith that form the hit set is exactly the 9 real sites, and the AC becomes satisfiable.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Part of this story has already landed — under a sibling ticket\n\n`_map_legacy_env` and `_LEGACY_ENV_ALIASES` **do not exist anywhere in `src`** on current main. They were deleted by `e096a33d3b7` *\"Delete the empty legacy env alias table\"*, which carries `rebar-ticket: 25a4-1ab3-3558-4cd4` — a sibling story in this same epic that landed **after** this plan was written.\n\nThe consequence is concrete: **`src/rebar/_config_sources.py` is 317 lines**, so all three cited ranges in it are past end-of-file and name content that no longer exists.\n\n| plan cites | status |\n|---|---|\n| `_config_sources.py:330-339` (delete the alias block) | **past EOF** — already deleted |\n| `_config_sources.py:342-352` (`env_overrides()`) | **past EOF** — now at `:296` |\n| `_config_sources.py:357-363` (policy default `warn`) | **past EOF** — now at `:312-317` |\n\nThat file now carries only prose about the removal (`:100`, `:300`, `:312`). **Whether `_config_sources.py` still belongs in Scope and `file_impact` is a real question** — the code change there is done, and only a possible docstring touch-up remains.\n\nThe Context paragraph's framing also needs updating: it says the three symbols are \"still threaded through five modules.\" Only `_ALIASES` is, and through **four** modules.\n\n---\n\n### 3. One citation would delete code the plan explicitly wants to keep\n\n> **Aliases.** Delete … `src/rebar/config.py:9,45,56` imports and `:382-385`\n\nOf those four locations, only `:9` is alias machinery. `config.py` (624 lines) contains **exactly one** alias reference:\n\n| cite | actual content at that line | verdict |\n|---|---|---|\n| `:9` | `from rebar._config_schema import _ALIASES as _ALIASES` | **correct** |\n| `:45` | `env_overrides,` | wrong — unrelated import |\n| `:56` | `resolve_acli_call_timeout as resolve_acli_call_timeout` | wrong — unrelated import |\n| `:382-385` | `raise_or_warn_env`, `raise_or_warn_file`, `tombstones` import + the `raise_or_warn_env(os.environ)` call | **wrong, and dangerous** |\n\n`:382-385` is the tombstone-raising machinery. This plan says to **keep** `REGISTRY`/`warn_deprecated`/`warn_deprecated_cfg_keys` as the future deprecation channel, and AC3 depends on `TICKETS_TRACKER_DIR=x rebar list` still failing loud. Deleting `:382-385` as instructed would break AC3 in the same change that asserts it.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Line drift in the surviving citations\n\n| plan cites | actual | content |\n|---|---|---|\n| `_config_sections.py:196-198` | `:198-200` | `_ALIASES` comment + definition |\n| `_config_sections.py:244-250` | `:245-250` | the alias loop |\n| `_config_sections.py:243` → rewrite | `:245` | `warn_deprecated_cfg_keys(...)` is the line to rewrite |\n| `_config_sections.py:209` (`_RESERVED_SECTIONS`) | `:211` | |\n| `_config_sections.py:224` (`continue`) | `:226` | |\n| `_deprecations.py:196-199` (`_tomb`) | `:127-129` | |\n| `_deprecations.py:209-217` (7 env rows) | `:211-217` is `raise_or_warn_env` | wrong region entirely |\n| `_deprecations.py:226,227,231,236,240,241` (6 cfg rows) | `:227-241` is `raise_or_warn_cfg_key` / `warn_deprecated_cfg_keys` | wrong region entirely |\n| `_deprecations.py:62` (`_MAJOR`) | `:27`; `_scheduled` at `:42` | |\n| `docs/config.md:410-413` (`[llm]` section) | that range is LLM `from_env()` prose | wrong region |\n| `scripts/gen_env_registry.py:484-488` (attribution comment) | that range is `main()` `--check` handling | wrong region |\n\n`docs/config.md` is 935 lines and `_deprecations.py` 335, so these are in-file but misaimed — the registry-row cites in particular point at *functions that consume* the rows, not the rows.\n\n---\n\n### 5. What I checked and found sound — do not \"fix\" these\n\nFour load-bearing claims verified true, so the review should not treat the drift above as impeaching the design:\n\n- **Tombstone census is exactly right.** `tombstones()` returns **19 rows: 6 `error` + 13 `warn`**, and every row carries `removed_in=\"v1.0.0\"`. The 6 error rows the plan names are precisely the 6 that exist (`TICKETS_TRACKER_DIR`, `REBAR_MCP_ALLOW_RECONCILE_LIVE`, `verify.require_verdict_for_close`, `.rebar/config.conf`, `REBAR_LLM_MAX_ITERS`, `REBAR_LLM_MODEL`). AC2's target state is reachable.\n- **The McCabe argument is correct, and it is the reason the two changes must ship together.** `coerce_sparse` measures **exactly 15** against a `max-complexity = 15` ceiling — it passes only because the gate fires at `> 15`. It is **not in `.github/complexity-baseline.json`**, so the ratchet does not freeze it; the live C901 ceiling is what binds. Adding the `[llm]` branch alone would push it to 16 and break `make lint`. Removing the alias loop first (−3) and then adding the branch lands at 13, matching the plan's own `coerce_sparse <= 13` assertion. Verified by lowering the threshold until it reported: `C901 'coerce_sparse' is too complex (15 > 6)`.\n- `scripts/gen_config_reference.py:224-233` → `_cfg_tombstones()`. **Exact.**\n- `docs/api-stability.md:27` → the alias sentence citing ADR 0116. **Exact.**\n- `_config_sections.py:22` → the `warn_deprecated` import to drop. **Exact.**\n\n---\n\n### Required before review\n\n1. **Rewrite AC1's grep** to bind whole identifiers and exclude `tests/fixtures`; state the expected post-change hit set (empty) rather than relying on the current form.\n2. **Re-scope for 25a4's landing** — drop the `_LEGACY_ENV_ALIASES`/`_map_legacy_env` deletion work, correct the Context's \"five modules,\" and decide whether `_config_sources.py` stays in Scope/`file_impact`.\n3. **Remove `config.py:45,56,382-385`** from the deletion list; `:9` is the only alias import.\n4. Re-point the `_deprecations.py` registry-row citations at the rows themselves, and fix the ~11 drifted line numbers above.\n\nThe tombstone design, the `[llm]` warn design, the sync test, and the complexity rationale all survive the sweep unchanged."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793423441494874619,"uuid":"61f3e0cf-b651-41dd-b4cf-214142284467"}